{{!-- "Other tags" — the sibling-subject strip under a tag archive.

	{{> "tag/other-tags" exclude=slug}}      called from inside {{#tag}}, so `slug` is this tag's

	exclude   the slug of the tag being read

The word is "other", so the tag the reader is already on is filtered out rather than listed
second. On this publication Interviews holds 21 posts and would otherwise rank second in its own
strip.

`filter="slug:-{{exclude}}"` is resolved by the get helper against the CURRENT context
(`parseOptions(ghostGlobals, this, …)` in core/frontend/helpers/get.js), and a partial's hash
arguments are merged into that context — so `exclude` is a plain path here and needs no `../`.
Plain and dotted paths are the only two shapes that resolver understands; `{{../slug}}` would
fail the render outright.

The section wrapper is inside the guard rather than at the call site: a publication filing
everything under one tag has no other tags, and an empty band with a heading over it is worse
than no band. --}}
{{#get "tags" include="count.posts" order="count.posts desc" limit="8" filter="slug:-{{exclude}}" as |tags|}}
	{{#if tags}}
		<section
			aria-labelledby="other-tags"
			class="container pt-18">
			{{> "tag-pills" tags=tags label=(t "Other tags") stacked=true headingId="other-tags"}}
		</section>
	{{/if}}
{{/get}}
